<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000T U.S. soybeans at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA buys 54,000T U.S. soybeans at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kaohsiung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. soybeans from Continental Grain Co at a tender on Friday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The association's Kaohsiung division comprises Great Wall Enterprise, Ttet Union, Prisedent Enterprise and Tai Hwa Oil.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type  Tonnes Date/Location		    Price/Futures</p>
<p>		  U.S. Gulf	 Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Soy   54,000 Feb 26-March 12 March 13-27  104.50 UScents/May</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
